{
  "name": "WF07_error_recovery",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## WF07 Responsibility\nScheduled and manual recovery share one state-aware, idempotent path.",
        "height": 180,
        "width": 430
      },
      "id": "a4b304e1-d5c8-4008-97c4-c0f604ced47f",
      "name": "WF07 Responsibility",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        16,
        208
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## DLQ Contract\nAutomatic runs select only pending work. Atomic claims move pending to reprocessing; outcomes are resolved, pending, or failed. Targeted manual recovery can return one failed row to pending without resetting attempt history.",
        "height": 180,
        "width": 430
      },
      "id": "f24e0ee8-8669-4f5c-8b2a-68c7596b95f5",
      "name": "DLQ Contract",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        480,
        208
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Failure Classification\nTimeout, rate-limit, network, and temporary provider errors are transient. Malformed or invalid input is permanent. Configuration and unknown failures require manual review.",
        "height": 180,
        "width": 430
      },
      "id": "9e4ca11d-a16b-4890-a3aa-d9f88a3327ed",
      "name": "Failure Classification",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        944,
        208
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Idempotent Replay Protection\nAll candidates, including targeted failed rows, pass through idempotency and persisted booking/follow-up checks. Completed operations resolve without repeated side effects.",
        "height": 180,
        "width": 430
      },
      "id": "a2404c48-4693-49e3-90b5-cfa0a5b81ace",
      "name": "Idempotent Replay Protection",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1408,
        208
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Retry / Backoff Policy\nMaximum 3 attempts. Failed transient work returns to pending for a later five-minute scheduler cycle. Exact exponential delay is deferred because no next_retry_at exists.",
        "height": 180,
        "width": 430
      },
      "id": "d7baa1a3-d82e-452a-b8cf-b9f92a5283de",
      "name": "Retry / Backoff Policy",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1856,
        208
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Recovery Operation Boundary\nExplicit simulated CRM/message/API handlers; booking/follow-up inspect persisted state.",
        "height": 180,
        "width": 430
      },
      "id": "cac38b5a-663f-4798-a4c5-3a124a3d8c02",
      "name": "Recovery Operation Boundary",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        2320,
        208
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Manual Reprocessing Safety\nConfigure manual_dlq_id in Prepare Manual Recovery Selection to target one pending or failed row; null selects oldest pending. Resolved and reprocessing rows are excluded. Replay protection always applies.",
        "height": 180,
        "width": 430
      },
      "id": "68c2c6a4-97a4-4279-9359-2f0f588f9574",
      "name": "Manual Reprocessing Safety",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        2784,
        208
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Audit Trail\nAudit events are inserted only for non-null lead_id.",
        "height": 180,
        "width": 430
      },
      "id": "24093a76-c379-4e1c-970a-ebf63dbadda0",
      "name": "Audit Trail",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        3248,
        208
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Known Limitations\nThe current DLQ schema has no claimed_at or lease_expires_at. If an execution crashes after claiming a row, it may remain in reprocessing and require operator intervention. Automatic stale-claim reset is intentionally not implemented because created_at is not a safe claim-age signal. Production should add claimed_at / lease_expires_at.",
        "height": 180,
        "width": 430
      },
      "id": "20d508f9-44a8-4cbc-8dca-09dc09a947c5",
      "name": "Known Limitations",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        3696,
        208
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Test Scope\nFuture coverage: T29 transient recovery, T30 exhaustion, T31 manual DLQ recovery, and T32 idempotent replay after partial success. No test-specific nodes are included.",
        "height": 180,
        "width": 430
      },
      "id": "a2c17efa-2daf-4e98-8de4-4dbf1c1a8491",
      "name": "Test Scope",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
